\section{Reaction Mechanism}
The reaction follows a Friedel-Crafts acylation of alkenes with oxygenates. The key steps involve:
1. \textbf{Acetal Formation:} The aldehyde reacts with the hydroxyl group of an alkene.
2. \textbf{Acylation:} A carbonyl group is attached to the alkene, forming an intermediate carbon-carbon bond.
3. \textbf{Acylation:} The carbonyl is transferred to the remaining carbon of the alkene to form the tetrafluorinated ketone.
4. \textbf{Rotation:} The four-membered ring (the 1,2-dihydro-substituted fragment) rotates anti-clockwise.
